OL,3,GNEWSAHiker died in 100ft fall from
OL,4,Aknife-edge ridge on Wales' highest
OL,5,Amountain
OL,6,
OL,7,FAn experienced hiker died after losing
OL,8,Fhis footing and falling 100ft from a
OL,9,Fknife-edge ridge on Wales' highest
OL,10,Fmountain.
OL,12,FAdrian McAnarney, 57, from County Down
OL,13,Fin Northern Ireland, had travelled with
OL,14,Fa group to Holyhead, to climb Yr
OL,15,FWyddfa, also known as Snowdon, and go
OL,16,Fsightseeing.
OL,18,FAn inquest in Caernarfon, Gwynedd, on
OL,19,FWednesday heard the carpenter fell from
OL,20,FCrib Goch, which reaches 3,028ft (923
OL,21,Fmetres), and died from multiple crush
OL,22,Finjuries on 2 August.
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,436,430,260,140,0,100
